content.text:
At 375x667, shop card bottom is cut off (build summary partially cut at bottom, maybe not fully visible) because content taller than viewport. The screenshot shows card from y~20 to 667, bottom "YOUR BUILD..." at 650 partially. It's not scrollable because panel is fixed and overflow hidden? `.game` overflow hidden, `.panel` grid place-items center. Card height ~ 648; viewport 667, it fits barely but bottom text cut by screenshot? The card bottom likely 667 and build summary 650, maybe visible fully? It shows "YOUR BUILD: ENGINE ★2 · CHASSIS ★3 · WHEELS ★2" wrapped, last line "★2" at bottom partly. The actions and text fit with 20 px margins. Fine. But on 320x568 it would overflow and be unreachable. Requirement mobile responsive. We should make panels scrollable on small screens with `overflow:auto` and align start on mobile, plus card margin. `.panel{... overflow:auto;}` and mobile `place-items:start center; padding:16px;` maybe. But fixed header? The card can scroll. Use `.panel{overflow-y:auto}` globally and on mobile `align-items:start`. `.panel` is grid place-items center; overflow auto with centered content could clip top if taller. On mobile, set `place-items:start center; padding:calc(16px + safe-area) 16px;` and `.card{margin:auto}`? If content taller than container, margin auto breaks? Better:
```
@media(max-width:700px){
.panel{display:block; overflow-y:auto; padding:calc(16px + env(safe-area-inset-top)) 16px calc(16px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)); background:...}
.card{width:min(510px,100%); margin:0 auto;}
}
```
But `display:block` and panel has hidden. Title card vertical center would be lost; use margin-top:auto? For portrait, top-aligned is okay. We can use flex:
```
.panel{display:flex; align-items:flex-start; justify-content:center; overflow-y:auto; padding:...}
```
The base `.panel{display:grid;place-items:center}`. Override to flex. Card no vertical center, top aligned. But on 844, title would top-align instead of centered; not ideal. Could use `align-items:safe center`? CSS `safe center` supported? `place-items:safe center` maybe. Simpler: keep grid center but set `.panel{overflow-y:auto}`. For content taller than viewport, CSS grid centering with overflow can clip top. To avoid, mobile use `align-content:start` with padding-top:max(22px, calc((100dvh - cardHeight)/2))? Not available.

Better use inner scroll: `.panel{overflow:auto}` and `.card{margin:auto}`. In grid container, `margin:auto` on grid item plus overflow auto will center if room, and top-align when overflow? With grid place-items center, the item is centered; if larger, negative overflow top. If we set `.panel{overflow:auto}` and card `margin:auto` and `place-items:stretch`? Hmm.

Use flex:
```
.panel{display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center; overflow-y:auto; padding:16px;}
.card{flex:0 0 auto; margin:auto 0;}
```
In a flex container with align-items:center and overflow, if item too tall, it overflows both top and bottom, scroll can reach bottom but top is clipped. Using `margin:auto` on the item in flex with `align-items:flex-start`? auto margins in flex axis can center when extra space and become 0 when no room. Yes: `.panel{display:flex;overflow-y:auto;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:center} .card{margin:auto 0}`. In a flex column? Panel flex direction row by default; align-items is cross-axis (vertical), margin auto vertical? For flex row, vertical auto margins center the item along cross-axis, and when item taller than container, auto margins resolve 0, starts at padding. That works. Set `.panel{display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:flex-start;overflow-y:auto}` and `.card{margin:auto 0}`. But base desktop currently grid; we could apply only mobile:
```
.panel{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:center;overflow-y:auto;padding:calc(16px + safe top) 16px calc(16px + safe bottom)}
.card{margin:auto 0;max-height:none}
```
With margin auto vertical, when card tall > container, top/bottom margins 0 and it starts at padding, scrolls. When short, centers. Good. Need ensure horizontal centering: justify-content center. Card width min(510px,94%) currently; mobile override width min(510,100%). At 375 with panel 16px padding, card width 343. Good.

Need apply to all panels mobile; title too. The title currently top 186 center; with this flex auto margins, still center when fits. Great.

Let's modify mobile `.panel` and `.card` width. Current mobile `.panel{background:...}` only. Add:
```
.panel{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:center;overflow-y:auto;padding:calc(16px + env(safe-area-inset-top)) 16px calc(16px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));background:...;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch}
.card{width:min(510px,100%);margin:auto 0;padding:23px 20px}
```
But `.card` base has padding 30; mobile has padding 23 20. Fine.
Does flex row with card margin auto 0 (top/bottom auto) center vertically? In flex container with align-items:flex-start, auto margins on cross-axis will absorb free space. Yes, if free space positive, both margins split; if negative, auto margins treated as 0 (I think). Should be okay.
Maybe use `margin-block:auto`.

Also the mobile shop at 375x667 after adding scroll would be fully accessible if taller. Good.

Need style for title. Let's patch and test at 320x568 maybe.

Also result card might be small. Fine.

Let's patch.

